{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"id\":\"N57\",\"lines\":\"rn-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N57.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"قَوَّٰمُونَ\",\"target_ar\":\"أَنفَقُوا۟\",\"after\":\"The market’s brisk trade makes the spending sound like resources circulating through an active economy. The verse’s material outflow becomes part of the image of support that keeps things moving.\",\"reason\":\"The rare market sense of قَوَّٰمُونَ is a market coming alive in sales, while أَنفَقُوا۟ means resources going out; the two make an image of economic circulation.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N57.2\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"قَوَّٰمُونَ\",\"target_ar\":\"فَٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتُ\",\"after\":\"A thriving market and sound women share a broad sense of things going well. The link is real but general.\",\"reason\":\"The market’s briskness in قَوَّٰمُونَ and the fitness or soundness of فَٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتُ meet only as positive states.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N58\",\"lines\":\"rr-r\"}\n{\"id\":\"N58.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"قَوَّٰمُونَ\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلرِّجَالُ\",\"after\":\"The bodily pain in the rare sense can settle in a limb. Heard with ٱلرِّجَالُ as a leg, the opening names the very kind of part in which pain can stand.\",\"reason\":\"قَوَّٰمُونَ can describe pain afflicting a body part, and ٱلرِّجَالُ is supplied here in its limb sense, الرِّجل.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N58.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"قَوَّٰمُونَ\",\"target_ar\":\"لِّلْغَيْبِ\",\"after\":\"The aching eye becomes the threshold of what remains unseen. The hidden is not abstract here: it is what the eye that hurts cannot disclose.\",\"reason\":\"The rare bodily-pain sense of قَوَّٰمُونَ includes قامت بي عيناي, “my eyes hurt”; لِّلْغَيْبِ names what is hidden from the eyes.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N58.4\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"قَوَّٰمُونَ\",\"target_ar\":\"وَٱضْرِبُوهُنَّ\",\"after\":\"A blow can make pain arise in the body. Heard together, the command carries the bodily consequence named by the rare sense.\",\"reason\":\"قَوَّٰمُونَ can mean that a bodily part gives pain, while وَٱضْرِبُوهُنَّ means striking; the blow and the pain it produces form one image.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N59\",\"lines\":\"r--\"}\n{\"id\":\"N59.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"قَوَّٰمُونَ\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلرِّجَالُ\",\"after\":\"The rare sense places a disease in the legs of sheep. With ٱلرِّجَالُ heard in its supplied limb sense, the verse echoes that same bodily site.\",\"reason\":\"The qiwām disease in قَوَّٰمُونَ affects a sheep’s limbs, and ٱلرِّجَالُ is glossed here as the leg, الرِّجل.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N60\",\"lines\":\"--rr\"}\n{\"id\":\"N60.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"قَوَّٰمُونَ\",\"target_ar\":\"لِّلْغَيْبِ\",\"after\":\"The hidden becomes what a sound-looking eye cannot see. The image makes absence visible as the limit of sight, even when the pupil remains intact.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense of قَوَّٰمُونَ is an eye that has lost sight despite a sound pupil; لِّلْغَيْبِ is what is hidden from the eyes.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N60.4\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"قَوَّٰمُونَ\",\"target_ar\":\"سَبِيلًا\",\"after\":\"The eye may be intact while its sight is gone, leaving the way unseen. The pairing makes a road present to the blind eye only as something it cannot follow by sight.\",\"reason\":\"قَوَّٰمُونَ carries the sense of an eye that no longer sees, while سَبِيلًا is a path to travel; lost sight makes that path inaccessible to view.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N61\",\"lines\":\"--rr\"}\n{\"id\":\"N61.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"حَفِظَ\",\"target_ar\":\"لِّلْغَيْبِ\",\"after\":\"Memory keeps present what is otherwise absent from awareness. Heard beside the hidden domain, preservation becomes the mind holding what is out of sight.\",\"reason\":\"حَفِظَ in its rare sense means retaining something in memory, while لِّلْغَيْبِ names what is hidden or absent from knowledge.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N61.4\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"حَفِظَ\",\"target_ar\":\"أَطَعْنَكُمْ\",\"after\":\"Remembering an instruction can be the stage that makes compliance possible. The verse’s obedience can thus be heard as a command retained and then acted upon.\",\"reason\":\"The memory sense of حَفِظَ preserves what was heard, and أَطَعْنَكُمْ is compliance; retention can serve as a stage of that compliance.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N62\",\"lines\":\"n-rnrrr-rr-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N62.1\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"حَفِظَ\",\"target_ar\":\"قَوَّٰمُونَ\",\"after\":\"Steady observance is something people carry out over time. The link to the male group named by قَوَّٰمُونَ is real but broad.\",\"reason\":\"حَفِظَ in this branch means keeping up an affair regularly, while قَوَّٰمُونَ is supplied as a group of men and their close circle.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N62.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"حَفِظَ\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱللَّهُ\",\"after\":\"The rare sense makes preservation a repeated practice. Beside ٱللَّهُ, that practice is heard as sustained worship rather than a single act.\",\"reason\":\"The regular observance in حَفِظَ and the worship sense named for ٱللَّهُ meet in ongoing religious devotion.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N62.4\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"حَفِظَ\",\"target_ar\":\"فَٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتُ\",\"after\":\"Sound conduct is strengthened by being maintained steadily. The relation is broad, since the words name a quality and its persistence.\",\"reason\":\"حَفِظَ means regular adherence, while فَٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتُ names sound or fitting women; constancy can sustain that soundness.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N62.5\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"حَفِظَ\",\"target_ar\":\"قَٰنِتَٰتٌ\",\"after\":\"Devotion and steadfast observance meet as a life of repeated religious practice. The verse’s obedient women are heard as constant in that devotion.\",\"reason\":\"The regular religious adherence of حَفِظَ and the devotional obedience of قَٰنِتَٰتٌ name the same sustained commitment.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N62.6\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"حَفِظَ\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱللَّهُ\",\"after\":\"Preserving an affair through repeated observance becomes a way of describing devotion to God. The divine name gathers that sustained practice into worship.\",\"reason\":\"حَفِظَ means keeping up a practice, and ٱللَّهُ is glossed with worship and the worshiped one; the repeated practice is religious observance.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N62.7\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"opposite\",\"focus_ar\":\"حَفِظَ\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلْمَضَاجِعِ\",\"after\":\"The rare sense stands for keeping up an affair, while the beds evoke lying down. Their contrast makes the verse’s constancy sound like rising to one’s duty instead of lapsing into idleness.\",\"reason\":\"حَفِظَ means persistent adherence, whereas ٱلْمَضَاجِعِ names places of lying on one’s side; constancy opposes slack repose.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N62.9\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"حَفِظَ\",\"target_ar\":\"أَطَعْنَكُمْ\",\"after\":\"Steady observance and compliance both describe continuing to follow an obligation. Heard together, the condition asks for adherence that lasts beyond a single moment.\",\"reason\":\"حَفِظَ in this branch means regular adherence, and أَطَعْنَكُمْ means compliance and obedience; both name sustained following.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N62.10\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"حَفِظَ\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱللَّهَ\",\"after\":\"The repeated practice of preservation is heard as a form of devotion to God. The closing name brings that constancy back to its object.\",\"reason\":\"The routine observance sense of حَفِظَ meets the worship sense attached to ٱللَّهَ as ongoing religious practice.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N63\",\"lines\":\"-rr\"}\n{\"id\":\"N63.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"حَفِظَ\",\"target_ar\":\"فَعِظُوهُنَّ\",\"after\":\"Admonition can awaken the attention needed to avoid a fall. The command to counsel becomes one means of making people vigilant.\",\"reason\":\"حَفَظَ’s rare sense here is alertness and few lapses, while فَعِظُوهُنَّ is cautionary counsel; counsel can produce vigilance.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N63.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"opposite\",\"focus_ar\":\"حَفِظَ\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلْمَضَاجِعِ\",\"after\":\"Alertness is set against lying down in the beds. The contrast makes vigilance the opposite of surrendering to repose.\",\"reason\":\"حَفَظَ in this branch means wakeful attention, whereas ٱلْمَضَاجِعِ names places of lying on one’s side.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N64\",\"lines\":\"-rnn\"}\n{\"id\":\"N64.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"حَفِظَ\",\"target_ar\":\"قَوَّٰمُونَ\",\"after\":\"The male group is pictured as standing in a protective charge. Their guardianship has the force of honor and zeal for what they defend.\",\"reason\":\"حَفَظَ can carry حفيظة, protective anger and honor, while قَوَّٰمُونَ names the group of men; together they picture men standing up for what they guard.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N64.3\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"حَفِظَ\",\"target_ar\":\"نُشُوزَهُنَّ\",\"after\":\"A rising or protrusion can provoke protective anger. The connection is plausible but depends on hearing the rise as a challenge.\",\"reason\":\"حَفَظَ in this branch means protective anger, and نُشُوزَهُنَّ is supplied as elevation or a protrusion that can stir that response.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N64.4\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"حَفِظَ\",\"target_ar\":\"فَعِظُوهُنَّ\",\"after\":\"Protective anger can find measured expression in admonition. The relation is real but general.\",\"reason\":\"The anger and zeal sense of حَفَظَ can prompt the corrective counsel named by فَعِظُوهُنَّ.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N65\",\"lines\":\"-r-rr-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N65.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"حَفَظَ\",\"target_ar\":\"قَوَّٰمُونَ\",\"after\":\"The male household group can be heard as the guardians of a covenant and its protected boundaries. The role is given the image of custodianship rather than mere presence.\",\"reason\":\"حَفَظَ in this branch means guarding sanctities, covenants, and fidelity; قَوَّٰمُونَ names the men and their close circle who can bear that guardianship.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N65.4\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"حَفَظَ\",\"target_ar\":\"لِّلْغَيْبِ\",\"after\":\"The covenant is kept precisely when its partner is absent. The hidden domain becomes the test of fidelity, where the unseen does not cancel the bond.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense of حَفَظَ includes keeping a husband’s covenant in his absence, while لِّلْغَيْبِ means absence or what is unseen.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N65.5\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"opposite\",\"focus_ar\":\"حَفَظَ\",\"target_ar\":\"وَٱضْرِبُوهُنَّ\",\"after\":\"Protection of sanctity and a blow pull in opposite directions. Heard together, the words make the command sequence carry a tension between guarding a person’s dignity and striking the person.\",\"reason\":\"حَفَظَ can mean preserving chastity, covenant, and protected boundaries, while وَٱضْرِبُوهُنَّ means striking them.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N66\",\"lines\":\"-nrr\"}\n{\"id\":\"N66.2\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"حَفِظَ\",\"target_ar\":\"تَخَافُونَ\",\"after\":\"A clear, unbroken way can answer apprehension about harm. The connection is plausible but not specific to this path.\",\"reason\":\"The rare حَفِظَ sense is a clear, straight road that does not break off, while تَخَافُونَ is apprehension of expected harm.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N66.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"حَفِظَ\",\"target_ar\":\"فَعِظُوهُنَّ\",\"after\":\"Counsel can direct a person onto a clear and unbroken way. The verse’s first response becomes guidance toward a preserved path.\",\"reason\":\"حَفِظَ names a straight, continuous road, and فَعِظُوهُنَّ is admonition that guides; the counsel complements the route.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N66.4\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"حَفِظَ\",\"target_ar\":\"سَبِيلًا\",\"after\":\"The rare branch gives a path that is clear, straight, and unbroken. سَبِيلًا names the way itself, so the two senses converge directly.\",\"reason\":\"حَفِظَ here means a straight, uninterrupted road, and سَبِيلًا is a road or path to travel.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N67\",\"lines\":\"--rr\"}\n{\"id\":\"N67.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱللَّهُ\",\"target_ar\":\"عَلِيًّا\",\"after\":\"The name used for calling upon God stands beside the predicate that declares Him high. The invocation and attribute complete one another in the verse’s divine coda.\",\"reason\":\"The rare ٱللَّهُ sense is the name used in oath and address, while عَلِيًّا means exalted or high; the invoked one is named by His height.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N67.4\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱللَّهُ\",\"target_ar\":\"كَبِيرًا\",\"after\":\"The divine name used in oath and address meets the attribute of greatness. The close makes the invoked God both personally named and beyond human scale.\",\"reason\":\"ٱللَّهُ in this branch is the name uttered in calling or swearing, and كَبِيرًا means immense and great; the name and attribute complete one another.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N68\",\"lines\":\"-rrrr-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N68.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"تَخَافُونَ\",\"target_ar\":\"فَعِظُوهُنَّ\",\"after\":\"The rare sense of making someone afraid meets the warning force of admonition. The counsel is heard as an attempt to make its danger felt.\",\"reason\":\"تَخَافُونَ can mean causing fear in another, and فَعِظُوهُنَّ is fear-inspiring admonition; both make danger present to the hearer.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N68.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"تَخَافُونَ\",\"target_ar\":\"وَٱضْرِبُوهُنَّ\",\"after\":\"Fear that is made to arise in others can culminate in the image of a blow. The two senses make the threat bodily and immediate.\",\"reason\":\"The rare تَخَافُونَ sense is to cause fear in someone, while وَٱضْرِبُوهُنَّ means to strike; a blow is an image of fear made concrete.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N68.4\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"opposite\",\"focus_ar\":\"تَخَافُونَ\",\"target_ar\":\"أَطَعْنَكُمْ\",\"after\":\"Fear imposed from outside stands against willing compliance. The rare sense makes the verse’s later obedience condition sound different from submission produced by fright.\",\"reason\":\"تَخَافُونَ can mean making another fear, whereas أَطَعْنَكُمْ is glossed as unforced compliance and obedience.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N68.5\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"تَخَافُونَ\",\"target_ar\":\"سَبِيلًا\",\"after\":\"The feared road becomes a route that makes people afraid. The image puts danger on the way itself, so pursuing a path can feel like entering a threat.\",\"reason\":\"The rare تَخَافُونَ sense makes fear arise in others; the dictionary image of a طريق مخوف, a feared road, meets سَبِيلًا as a path.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N69\",\"lines\":\"---n\"}\n{\"id\":\"N69.4\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"تَخَافُونَ\",\"target_ar\":\"كَبِيرًا\",\"after\":\"Outdoing another in fear implies a greater degree of fear. The link to greatness is a shared scale of intensity, so it stays general.\",\"reason\":\"تَخَافُونَ in this branch means overcoming someone in fear, while كَبِيرًا names greatness or immensity.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N70\",\"lines\":\"rro-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N70.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"opposite\",\"focus_ar\":\"تَخَافُونَ\",\"target_ar\":\"فَضَّلَ\",\"after\":\"The rare sense takes something away or reduces it; فَضَّلَ carries the image of excess or remainder. The pair sets diminution against surplus within the verse’s account of allocation.\",\"reason\":\"تَخَافُونَ can mean diminishing a thing, while فَضَّلَ is glossed here as increase and remainder; the senses oppose one another.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N70.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"تَخَافُونَ\",\"target_ar\":\"أَنفَقُوا۟\",\"after\":\"Taking away from a thing meets the outflow of spending. The two senses make the resources named in the verse appear as something reduced by leaving their source.\",\"reason\":\"The rare تخوّف sense of تَخَافُونَ is depletion, and أَنفَقُوا۟ means resources going out or being spent; both describe diminution by outflow.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N70.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"opposite\",\"focus_ar\":\"تَخَافُونَ\",\"target_ar\":\"نُشُوزَهُنَّ\",\"after\":\"Reduction is set against elevation and protrusion. The pairing makes the two senses move in opposite spatial directions.\",\"reason\":\"تَخَافُونَ in this branch means taking away or diminishing, whereas نُشُوزَهُنَّ is glossed as rising or protruding.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N71\",\"lines\":\"n----\"}\n{\"id\":\"N71.1\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"تَخَافُونَ\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلرِّجَالُ\",\"after\":\"Fear can show itself through the body, including its limbs. The link to the leg sense of ٱلرِّجَالُ is plausible but broad.\",\"reason\":\"The rare تَخَافُونَ sense is fear appearing outwardly on a person, while ٱلرِّجَالُ is supplied in its limb sense; a leg can be one site of that display.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N72\",\"lines\":\"-r-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N72.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"تَخَافُونَ\",\"target_ar\":\"لِّلْغَيْبِ\",\"after\":\"A leather pouch carries something out of sight. The hidden domain becomes an object concealed inside the carrier’s bag.\",\"reason\":\"The rare خافة sense at تَخَافُونَ is a leather honey pouch or outer garment, while لِّلْغَيْبِ names what is hidden from view.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N73\",\"lines\":\"rnr-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N73.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"نُشُوزَهُنَّ\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلرِّجَالُ\",\"after\":\"Rising from a seat takes the legs into action. Heard with ٱلرِّجَالُ as a leg, the bodily part is present in the movement the rare sense names.\",\"reason\":\"نُشُوزَهُنَّ in this branch means getting up and moving from a seat, while ٱلرِّجَالُ is supplied as the limb الرِّجل, part of standing.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N73.2\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"نُشُوزَهُنَّ\",\"target_ar\":\"قَوَّٰمُونَ\",\"after\":\"A group of people can rise from its place. The connection is clear but generic because قَوَّٰمُونَ is supplied here as a male group.\",\"reason\":\"نُشُوزَهُنَّ can mean rising from a seat, while قَوَّٰمُونَ names a group of men; the image is of people getting up.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N73.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"opposite\",\"focus_ar\":\"نُشُوزَهُنَّ\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلْمَضَاجِعِ\",\"after\":\"Getting up from a seat stands against lying down in the beds. The two bodily postures make a direct vertical contrast in the response sequence.\",\"reason\":\"نُشُوزَهُنَّ in this branch means rising and leaving a seat, whereas ٱلْمَضَاجِعِ names places of lying on one’s side.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N74\",\"lines\":\"nrrrr\"}\n{\"id\":\"N74.1\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"نُشُوزَهُنَّ\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلنِّسَآءِ\",\"after\":\"Marital aversion is a state attributed to women in this clause. The connection is real but simply one of class and member.\",\"reason\":\"The rare نُشُوزَهُنَّ sense describes estrangement between spouses, while ٱلنِّسَآءِ names the women’s group that includes the specified wives.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N74.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"opposite\",\"focus_ar\":\"نُشُوزَهُنَّ\",\"target_ar\":\"قَٰنِتَٰتٌ\",\"after\":\"Aversion to the spouse and refusal of obedience stand against devoted submission. The verse’s positive profile and feared discord become opposing relational states.\",\"reason\":\"نُشُوزَهُنَّ can mean aversion to the husband and raising oneself from obedience, while قَٰنِتَٰتٌ means religiously devoted obedience.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N74.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"نُشُوزَهُنَّ\",\"target_ar\":\"وَٱهْجُرُوهُنَّ\",\"after\":\"Marital estrangement meets the command to separate. The rare sense names the relational fracture, and the imperative gives that distance an action.\",\"reason\":\"نُشُوزَهُنَّ in this branch means spouses’ aversion or estrangement, and وَٱهْجُرُوهُنَّ means to separate from them.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N74.4\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"نُشُوزَهُنَّ\",\"target_ar\":\"وَٱضْرِبُوهُنَّ\",\"after\":\"Spousal aversion and a blow make a picture of conflict becoming bodily. The rare sense supplies the relational rupture around which the striking command is heard.\",\"reason\":\"نُشُوزَهُنَّ can mean mutual marital aversion, while وَٱضْرِبُوهُنَّ means striking; together they depict an escalating conflict.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N74.5\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"نُشُوزَهُنَّ\",\"target_ar\":\"عَلِيًّا\",\"after\":\"A spouse’s relational rising is heard beneath God’s true height. The coda places household conflict under a scale of elevation that belongs ultimately to God.\",\"reason\":\"The rare نُشُوزَهُنَّ sense includes raising oneself above a spouse’s obedience, while عَلِيًّا means exalted and high; the pair makes a contrast of human and divine elevation.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N75\",\"lines\":\"rnn\"}\n{\"id\":\"N75.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"نُشُوزَهُنَّ\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلرِّجَالُ\",\"after\":\"Speech that makes someone stand brings the legs into motion. The bodily limb supplies a part of the rising named in the rare sense.\",\"reason\":\"نُشُوزَهُنَّ in this branch means angering someone and making him stand by speech, while ٱلرِّجَالُ is supplied as the leg, الرِّجل.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N75.2\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"نُشُوزَهُنَّ\",\"target_ar\":\"قَوَّٰمُونَ\",\"after\":\"A spoken provocation can make people get up. The image touches the male group named by قَوَّٰمُونَ, though the relation is broad.\",\"reason\":\"The rare نُشُوزَهُنَّ sense includes speech that raises someone to standing, while قَوَّٰمُونَ is glossed as a group of men and kin.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N75.3\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"نُشُوزَهُنَّ\",\"target_ar\":\"حَٰفِظَٰتٌ\",\"after\":\"Provoked anger can arise around what someone is guarding. The connection is plausible but depends on hearing the anger as protective.\",\"reason\":\"نُشُوزَهُنَّ can mean angering someone by speech, while حَٰفِظَٰتٌ names ongoing guardianship; insult to what is guarded can provoke anger.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N76\",\"lines\":\"---\"}\n{\"id\":\"N77\",\"lines\":\"-n-n\"}\n{\"id\":\"N77.2\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"نُشُوزَهُنَّ\",\"target_ar\":\"قَوَّٰمُونَ\",\"after\":\"A strong, mature man belongs to the male group named by قَوَّٰمُونَ. The relation is one of member and group rather than a fuller shared image.\",\"reason\":\"نُشُوزَهُنَّ in this branch describes a man retaining strength in age, while قَوَّٰمُونَ is supplied as a group of men and their close circle.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N77.4\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"نُشُوزَهُنَّ\",\"target_ar\":\"كَبِيرًا\",\"after\":\"The mature man at full age and strength approaches the broad scale of greatness. The connection is a general one of attained stature.\",\"reason\":\"نُشُوزَهُنَّ here describes a man who has reached his age and strength, while كَبِيرًا means great or immense.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N78\",\"lines\":\"----\"}\n{\"id\":\"N79\",\"lines\":\"-r-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N79.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"opposite\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَٱهْجُرُوهُنَّ\",\"target_ar\":\"قَٰنِتَٰتٌ\",\"after\":\"The rare sense of obscene speech stands against devotional obedience. The women’s piety makes indecent language sound like the conduct to be left behind.\",\"reason\":\"وَٱهْجُرُوهُنَّ can carry the sense of foul or indecent speech, while قَٰنِتَٰتٌ names submissive religious devotion.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N80\",\"lines\":\"-rr-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N80.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَٱهْجُرُوهُنَّ\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلْمَضَاجِعِ\",\"after\":\"The bed becomes the setting of a patient’s delirium or a sleeper’s rambling. The rare sense gives the lying place a disordered voice.\",\"reason\":\"وَٱهْجُرُوهُنَّ in this branch means involuntary delirium in sickness or sleep, while ٱلْمَضَاجِعِ names places of lying down.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N80.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"opposite\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَٱهْجُرُوهُنَّ\",\"target_ar\":\"أَطَعْنَكُمْ\",\"after\":\"Involuntary, disordered speech contrasts with deliberate compliance. The condition of obedience is heard as an answer to conduct that lacks conscious direction.\",\"reason\":\"وَٱهْجُرُوهُنَّ can mean unintentional delirium, whereas أَطَعْنَكُمْ is willing compliance and obedience.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N81\",\"lines\":\"-nn\"}\n{\"id\":\"N81.2\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَٱهْجُرُوهُنَّ\",\"target_ar\":\"قَوَّٰمُونَ\",\"after\":\"The midday heat can halt travel and activity. That pause is loosely connected to the standing or active group named by قَوَّٰمُونَ.\",\"reason\":\"وَٱهْجُرُوهُنَّ in this branch can mean the hot noon when people stop traveling, while قَوَّٰمُونَ is supplied as a group of men.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N81.3\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَٱهْجُرُوهُنَّ\",\"target_ar\":\"كَبِيرًا\",\"after\":\"The heat of midday can be intense, and كَبِيرًا names greatness or immensity. Their link is a broad scale of magnitude.\",\"reason\":\"وَٱهْجُرُوهُنَّ can mean the fierce heat of midday, while كَبِيرًا means immense or great.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N82\",\"lines\":\"nr--\"}\n{\"id\":\"N82.1\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَٱهْجُرُوهُنَّ\",\"target_ar\":\"قَوَّٰمُونَ\",\"after\":\"Men can be the people who set out at the first hour. The pairing is real but generic: one sense names the group, the other their early departure.\",\"reason\":\"وَٱهْجُرُوهُنَّ in this branch means going early at the start of a time, while قَوَّٰمُونَ is supplied as a group of men.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N82.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَٱهْجُرُوهُنَّ\",\"target_ar\":\"أَنفَقُوا۟\",\"after\":\"The rare sense is people leaving early, while spending is wealth going out. The verse’s departure of people and outflow of resources make parallel movements away from a source.\",\"reason\":\"وَٱهْجُرُوهُنَّ can mean setting out at the beginning of a time, and أَنفَقُوا۟ means causing resources to go out; both make an image of departure.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N83\",\"lines\":\"rr--\"}\n{\"id\":\"N83.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَٱهْجُرُوهُنَّ\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلرِّجَالُ\",\"after\":\"The tether binds an animal’s limb. Heard with ٱلرِّجَالُ as a leg, the target names the very part the rope holds.\",\"reason\":\"وَٱهْجُرُوهُنَّ in this branch is a rope tied around a camel’s leg or wrist, while ٱلرِّجَالُ is supplied as the leg, الرِّجل.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N83.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَٱهْجُرُوهُنَّ\",\"target_ar\":\"وَٱضْرِبُوهُنَّ\",\"after\":\"A tether restrains a body, and a blow lands on it. Together the rare rope sense and the striking command make a stark image of restraint followed by impact.\",\"reason\":\"وَٱهْجُرُوهُنَّ can mean a cord binding an animal’s limb, while وَٱضْرِبُوهُنَّ means striking; their senses form a restraint-and-blow image.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N84\",\"lines\":\"-rrr\"}\n{\"id\":\"N84.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَٱهْجُرُوهُنَّ\",\"target_ar\":\"فَٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتُ\",\"after\":\"The rare sense describes unmatched beauty and completeness. Beside the sound or fitting women, it intensifies the verse’s language of excellence.\",\"reason\":\"وَٱهْجُرُوهُنَّ can carry the sense of surpassing others in beauty and perfection, while فَٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتُ names what is sound and fitting.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N84.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَٱهْجُرُوهُنَّ\",\"target_ar\":\"عَلِيًّا\",\"after\":\"The rare sense includes a palm exceeding others in height. عَلِيًّا names highness, so the two senses meet in the image of surpassing elevation.\",\"reason\":\"وَٱهْجُرُوهُنَّ can describe something surpassing its measure in height, and عَلِيًّا means elevated or high.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N84.4\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَٱهْجُرُوهُنَّ\",\"target_ar\":\"كَبِيرًا\",\"after\":\"Unmatched completeness carries a sense of exceeding ordinary measure. Beside كَبِيرًا, that excellence takes on the scale of greatness.\",\"reason\":\"وَٱهْجُرُوهُنَّ can mean surpassing one’s counterparts in perfection, while كَبِيرًا means great or immense.\"}"}}
